.TH AOCD 8 "2026-11-08" "acer-open-control 0.3.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
aocd \- AcerOpenControl daemon for Clevo-based Acer laptops
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aocd
.RB [ \-\-socket
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-models
.IR dir ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aocd
controls fan speed, keyboard backlight, performance profile, battery charge
limit, webcam power and Fn hotkeys through the laptop firmware's WMBB WMI
method, using the acpi_call kernel module. It is normally started by systemd
as
.BR aocd.service .
Laptop support comes from model profiles; with no matching profile the daemon
runs read-only. When it stops, fans are handed back to the BIOS.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-socket " path"
Control socket (default /run/acer-open-control/aocd.sock).
.TP
.BI \-\-config " path"
Settings file (default /etc/acer-open-control/config.json).
.TP
.BI \-\-models " dir"
Load model profiles from this directory only.
.SH FILES
/usr/share/acer-open-control/models/*.toml, /etc/acer-open-control/models.d/*.toml,
/etc/acer-open-control/config.json
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aocctl (1),
.BR aoc-gtk (1),
/usr/share/doc/acer-open-control/
